---
description: Building or changing screens. Use the shared component library and the T&T theme.
globs: app/**/*.tsx, components/**/*.tsx
---

- Build screens from `@/components/library`. Do not create a one-off button, input, card, table or status pill.
- A screen leads with its job: page title, then the next action or the decision, then the evidence. One primary action in that region.
- Colours come from the `asm-*` Tailwind utilities (`styles/library-theme.css`). Never write a hex value outside `styles/tokens.css`.
- shadcn primitives, when added, live under `components/ui`, take their colour from Assemble tokens, and are wrapped by the library. A page does not import them. Do not paste a default shadcn theme into a component.
- Wrap a new screen in `asm-root`.
- Engagement status uses `DeliveryStatus` (glyph, label and wash). Other short states use `Badge` with words.
- Comparison tables use `Table`. The figure appears once. Actions stay on one row.
- Empty, loading and failed each get a sentence and one action. Use `EmptyState` for an empty list, not for a failed request.
- Every string comes from `lib/copy.ts` with a Welsh equivalent in `lib/copy.cy.ts`.
- Engagement screens read `trpc.spine.get` and invalidate `spine.get` and `spine.board` after a mutation.
- A new library component needs a guide in `components/library/guides.ts` and an example in `Catalogue.tsx`. The guide states the user need, when not to use it, and the hit size.
- When you touch a screen that still uses `btn-teach` or another one-off action class, replace those actions with `Button` or `ButtonLink`.
- Reference: `docs/redesign/README.md`.
